add(678,[626],[48],'1261','On peut généraliser ... hypothèse ... i≤i0 ... conclusion ... j≥2d−i0.','The claimed partial transfer of local constancy from R^if!F for i≤i0 to the complementary ordinary-image range is false in general, even with smooth compactifiable f and a constant finite field coefficient sheaf. The all-degree version CL-SA12-651 is the safe refinement.','false as stated without additional hypotheses','New independent counterexample: overC putj:G_m→A¹, p:G_m×A¹→G_m andf=jp. All maps are separated finite type; f is smooth pure relative dimensiond1 and compactifiable byP¹×A¹ overA¹. ForΛ=Fℓ,ℓ any prime, F=Λ is locally constant free rank1 andℓ invertible. A¹ has ordinary cohomologyΛ in degree0 and compact-support cohomologyΛ(−1) in degree2. ThusRf!Λ=j!Λ(−1)[−2] andRf_*Λ=Rj_*Λ. ConsequentlyR0f!Λ=R1f!Λ=0 are locally constant, butR1f_*Λ(1)=i_*Λ, i:{0}→A¹, is not locally constant. Takei0=1:2d−i0=1. Alsoj_*Λ=Λ andR1j_*Λ=i_*Λ(−1). A surjective variant adds the disjoint productA¹×A¹→A¹; the same failure remains. See programs/exact_checks.py output for degree bookkeeping and review.md for the geometric proof.','F','Searches of SGA4 XVIII3.2 and relative local-constancy sources found the all-degree duality theorem, not a published theorem with this unrestricted partial implication. Riou3.1.3 provides the exact punctured-line direct-image calculation; the counterexample is new in this review.','No exact published form of the partial sentence identified. Counterexample checked19November2026.','Refuted literally; do not mark the source note as merely a successful inequality check. The source has no surjectivity hypothesis; even that added condition would not fix the example.',['SA12_SGA4III','SA12_Riou2014','SA12_Milne2013'],[13,14,28,29,30,31])
