  c['his_statement']='For every torsion sheaf F on a scheme locally algebraic over C, H^q(X,F)→H^q(Xan,Fan) is an isomorphism; relative finite-type comparison follows.'
  c['status_on_pages']='stated without proof; false under the literal unrestricted nonproper every-torsion reading'
  c['computation']='New independent counterexample: X=A¹_C, Λ=Fℓ, and F=⊕_{m∈Z}i_{m*}Λ for the closed integer points. On the quasi-compact algebraic étale site, a section of the sheaf direct sum is supported in finitely many summands, so H0(X,F)=⊕_ZΛ. Analytification preserves colimits; the integer set is closed discrete in C, so arbitrary choices at all integer points are locally finite sections of the analytic direct sum, giving H0(Xan,Fan)=∏_ZΛ. The comparison is the strict direct-sum inclusion. All sheaves are killed byℓ and X is smooth affine finite type; F is not constructible. This argument uses no numerical computation.'
  c['fate']='SGA4 XVI4.1 explicitly assumes either f proper or F constructible. This proves the corrected formulation in the statement field and does not prove the literal every-torsion assertion. The counterexample is an independent reconstruction of this review.'
  c['present_status']='As of November2026: the constructible-torsion comparison is established; the literal unrestricted nonproper wording is refuted. Check the ink or an inherited constructibility convention before attributing an authorial error.'
